{
    "chapter_num": 20,
    "verses_count": 8,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Rabbah Is Conquered"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "It happened "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Lit. at the return of the year"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "in the spring of the year, at the time kings go out "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "to battle,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " that Joab led out the armed forces and ravaged the country of the people of Ammon, and came and besieged Rabbah. But David stayed at Jerusalem. And Joab defeated Rabbah and overthrew it. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Then David took their king’s crown from his head, and found it to weigh a talent of gold, and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "there were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " precious stones in it. And it was set on David’s head. Also he brought out the "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "plunder"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "spoil of the city in great abundance. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "And he brought out the people who "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "were"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in it, and "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "LXX cut them with"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "put "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "them"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " to work with saws, with iron picks, and with axes. So David did to all the cities of the people of Ammon. Then David and all the people returned "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "to"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Jerusalem."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Philistine Giants Destroyed"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Now it happened afterward that war broke out at "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gob, 2 Sam. 21:18"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Gezer with the Philistines, at which time Sibbechai the Hushathite killed "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Saph, 2 Sam. 21:18"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Sippai, "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "who was one"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " of the sons of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or Raphah"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "the giant. And they were subdued."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Again there was war with the Philistines, and Elhanan the son of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Jaare-Oregim, 2 Sam. 21:19"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Jair killed Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the shaft of whose spear "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "was"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " like a weaver’s beam."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Yet again there was war at Gath, where there was a man of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "great"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " stature, with twenty-four fingers and toes, six "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "on each hand"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and six "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "ITALIC",
                            "text": "on each foot;"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " and he also was born to "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or Raphah"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "the giant. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "So when he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of "
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Shammah, 1 Sam. 16:9 or Shimeah, 2 Sam. 21:21"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Shimea, David’s brother, killed him."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "These were born to the giant in Gath, and they fell by the hand of David and by the hand of his servants."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}